1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:01,458
Why the salt bridge?

2
00:00:01,458 --> 00:00:08,268
The zinc side keeps gaining positive zinc ions, and the copper side keeps losing positive copper ions.

3
00:00:08,268 --> 00:00:11,718
Charge would build up and stop the cell in a moment.

4
00:00:11,718 --> 00:00:18,710
The bridge sends negative chloride ions towards the zinc side and positive potassium ions towards the copper side.

5
00:00:18,710 --> 00:00:23,958
It completes the circuit, keeps both solutions neutral, and stops them mixing.

